{"kind":"assert","text":"Review finding for exact binding candidate4258167d01d6339bfd67c60047cb2afae60ce891: explicit implementation selectors can hide obligations of examined reporting companions. In [resolveAssigned](internal/reviewguard/binding.go@4258167d01d6339bfd67c60047cb2afae60ce891:243), the selector branch includes only selected commitments even when another examined artifact reports another implementation. [validateLanding](cmd/gs/main.go@4258167d01d6339bfd67c60047cb2afae60ce891:1247) then checks only that subset, while the merge still lands the whole candidate.\n\nIndependent actual-command controls derived from the candidate's combined-delivery fixture confirm both cases. First/second artifacts are both explicitly examined, first is the primary, but --implementation selects only first. With second held, gs merge succeeds instead of the combined-held refusal. With second owed to refs/heads/other, gs review and gs merge still succeed into main. The corresponding controls without a selector correctly refuse the held companion at merge and the different destination at review. Four controls ran together in9.217s: both omission cases red, both positive refusals green. The held example is specifically a bypass of the combined-held guard; existing single-hold compatibility warnings are not reinterpreted as an absolute block. Test source and complete output attached.\n\nKeep the correction on #19651. A selector may disambiguate an examined report's lifecycle but must not suppress other examined delivery reports or their target/hold constraints. Use one complete resolved set consistently for confirmation, admission, preparation, authorization, merge and receipt explanation. Add meaningful omission controls through real commands; do not sweep uncited artifacts at the head or add ancestry inference. Publish a corrected exact head and fresh independent review. This head must not merge on an approval that overlooks this defect.\n\nArchitecture: the layer7 contract is documented, but this subset behavior contradicts its claim to classify the explicitly examined reporting set. Security: reproduced destination/hold guard bypass is unresolved. Simplification: retain the single shared resolver; make selector semantics narrow and complete instead of adding a compensating second sweep in each consumer. Existing reviewguard and mergeplan package suites passed independently (0.341s and3.780s), but did not catch these omission cases. Full approval is withheld; review intake19702's ordinary-stale basis reconciliation remains with its author.\n","body":{"head":"4258167d01d6339bfd67c60047cb2afae60ce891","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:468f2a146c06bcace7138c1000273e264037a6bb, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:cc63bec115eb46f871efc03f9a7f0d8b965d018a stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:001b2e3b06105d22946682cb90201bc66c1c6a26, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:01ab55ec50e015756b4e4e1c274259f118956c9f, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:02a7302bf06f4f95ea67698d571fd7470055d448, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:02a980f84e17c4f9b9e5dc91e01e963a2f39c53d and 88 more"}}